  "keyFindings": {
    "headlessDiscrepancyRootCause": "In headless mode with --disable-renderer-backgrounding and --disable-background-timer-throttling, Chromium operates without hardware V-Sync synchronization. The benchmark probe scripts (RAF_SCRIPT, FT_SCRIPT, and LT_SCRIPT) repeatedly queued high-frequency frame tracking callbacks (240 consecutive RAFs) directly into Chromium compositor queues. In genuine headed Chromium, the main thread CPU time is only ~63-79ms per second (<8% of one core), with 0 long tasks (>50ms) across all idle and visible scenarios.",
    "userPerceivedSmoothness": "R4.2 is measurably smoother than R4.1 in all real user interactions. Continuous scroll (H4) shows a 21.0% task reduction and a 48.5% paint reduction. Planet hover (H5) shows a 15.9% task reduction and 19.1% style recalculation reduction. Pointer interaction shows 26% lower task time under burst instrumentation with 0 long tasks.",
    "reconciliationVerdict": "The historical headless TaskDuration inflation was entirely benchmark-harness and headless-scheduling induced. R4.2 delivers superior real-world performance, verified in genuine headed Chromium traces."
  }
